    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0083" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.852/27: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-10T13:00:00-06:00">October 10, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. Suarez advised October 9, that in reference to his offer to purchase the two
                    German tankers now in Mexican ports the German Legation told him that its answer
                    to his proposal would be delayed until the outcome of Hitler’s peace proposals
                    became evident. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
